## Virtual environment (from SlideMage's PySide6 migration). Machine-specific, never meant to be
## committed -- kept here as a legacy-path safety net only. As of
## 2026-08-11, the real venv no longer lives inside the project folder at
## all: this whole folder is Dropbox/SyncBackPro-synced, and a venv is
## tens of thousands of small files whose absolute interpreter path is
## baked in per-machine anyway (confirmed directly: a venv synced over
## from a second PC pointed at a python.exe that doesn't exist here and
## failed outright; the sync clients also locked/indexed its files badly
## enough that even deleting it repeatedly timed out). The venv now lives
## machine-locally at `%USERPROFILE%\SlideMaster\venv` (not
## `%LOCALAPPDATA%` -- that's virtualized per-app on a machine whose
## system Python is the Microsoft Store package, which silently broke venv
## isolation entirely; confirmed directly, 2026-08-11), outside any synced
## folder, one real venv per machine, auto-created/auto-migrated by
## `SlideMage.bat` on first run -- see its own comments. This `.venv/`
## entry just stays as a guard in case one ever gets created here again by
## habit (e.g. `python -m venv .venv` run by hand).
.venv/

## Python build output (`pip wheel`/`python -m build`).
build/
dist/

## SlideMage's slide-source editor: a local undo net (full timestamped
## history, kept per slide file) for its own saves -- not meant to be
## committed (2026-07-23):
**/slides/.backups/

## RStudio per-user session state (R_Slidemaster/), untracked 2026-07-27,
## direct instruction. `.Rproj.user/` is RStudio's own scratch state --
## pane layouts, breakpoints, and cached copies of open/unsaved editor
## buffers (`sources/per/t/*-contents`) -- and is gitignored by RStudio's
## own project template; 24 of its files plus three `.Rhistory` console
## logs had nevertheless been committed here. The project file itself
## (`R_Slidemaster/R_Slidemaster.Rproj`) stays tracked, as is conventional,
## and so does every real package file (DESCRIPTION/NAMESPACE/LICENSE/
## R/*.R/man/*.Rd). `.RData`/`.Ruserdata` are listed pre-emptively: same
## category, not currently present.
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata

# Accessibility outputs: generated on demand, never committed (see
# ALT_TEXT_NOTES.md). Transcripts are regenerated from the deck + slide
# files + media/alt-text.json; the bake-off is a one-off model comparison.
transcripts/
alt-text-bakeoff.md

# Compile-time slide preview PNGs (slide_snapshot.py) -- a best-effort
# cache refreshed opportunistically on every compile that touches a slide,
# not a build artifact worth keeping in history. Moved under previews/
# 2026-09-18 (was a project-root folder before that), then under .previews/
# the same day (dot-prefixed: nothing the user needs to interact with).
**/.previews/slide_previews/

# Rendered PNGs of .pdf media (media_render.py, 2026-08-26) -- same
# regeneratable-cache reasoning as slide_previews/ above, for the Images
# tab's own preview and Ollama drafting, both of which need a raster image
# a .pdf media file itself isn't. Moved under previews/ 2026-09-18, then
# .previews/ the same day (was a project-root folder before that).
**/.previews/pdf_render_cache/

# Rendered/cropped PNGs of \tikzillustration{} bodies (tikz_render.py) --
# same regeneratable-cache reasoning again: entirely derived, on demand,
# from a slide's own current tikz source, for the Images tab's preview and
# Ollama drafting of a hand-drawn diagram that has no media/ file at all.
# Moved under previews/ 2026-09-18, then .previews/ the same day (was a
# project-root folder before that).
**/.previews/tikz_illustration_previews/

# Persistent preview maintenance lock and local, checksummed benchmark evidence.
**/.previews/preview-maintenance.lock
# Background renders (render_store.py): shared objects, regenerable
**/.previews/render-store/
**/.previews/benchmarks/

# SlideMage's own local UI preferences (app_settings.py -- currently
# just dark mode) -- a personal taste, not project content worth
# version-controlling/diffing on every toggle, same category as
# .claude/settings.local.json above. Still a plain file physically inside
# the project's .slidemage/ (not the Windows registry), so the folder's own cloud-sync
# client -- not git -- carries it across machines; see dist/ above for the
# identical git-ignored-but-not-sync-ignored precedent.
**/.slidemage/app_settings.json
# How many passes each deck's compile needed last time (compile_passes.py):
# rewritten by compiles, only a progress estimate.
**/.slidemage/compile_passes.json
# A slide's text before its last AI edit (ai_review.last_before), for Compare rendered: a local cache,
# one file per slide, overwritten by the next AI edit.
**/.slidemage/ai-before/

## Scratch folder for source PDFs/pptx used while converting slides (large,
## machine-local, never meant to be committed).
.temp/

# Written by SlideMage on opening the demo project (project format guard,
# v4.1.0); a new project gets its own on first open.
example/.slidemage/project.json

# Reusable single-slide preview wrappers (safe to remove with build output).
**/decks/_slidemage_preview-*.tex
